  "ingredients": [
    "1.6666666269302 cups milk",
    "3 large eggs",
    "2 cups all-purpose flour",
    "2.25 teaspoons baking powder",
    "0.5 teaspoon salt",
    "0.25 cup melted butter",
    "0.66666668653488 cup blueberries",
    "1.5 cups blueberries",
    "3 T honey",
    "1/2 c orange juice",
    "1 T cornstarch"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Make the waffles: In a medium bowl, whisk together milk and egg yolks. Stir in flour, baking powder, and salt. Stir in melted butter and let stand for about 30 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Lightly grease and preheat a waffle iron according to the manufacturer’s instructions.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Beat egg whites in a glass, metal, or ceramic bowl until stiff. Fold into batter with blueberries.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Working in batches, scoop portions of the batter onto the preheated waffle iron. Cook each waffle until golden brown and the iron stops steaming, 4 to 6 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, make the sauce: Stir blueberries, 1/4 cup orange juice, and honey together in a medium saucepan over medium heat. Bring to a boil.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix remaining 1/4 cup orange juice and cornstarch together in a small bowl; stir into the blueberry mixture. Cook, stirring constantly, until thickened. Serve warm over waffles.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    }
  ],
